      "message": "fix(multiaxis): rotary operations read a face selection or refuse it\n\nA rotary operation whose source was a face selection cut the whole\nmodel without a message: `material_of` reads a selection as the full\nfacets of the picked models, and no rotary arm read the picks.\n\nRotary Parallel now keeps its cut over the picked faces. The raster\nis planned on the whole model, as before, and each cut point is kept\nwhere the radial through the ball centre meets a picked facet\n(`multiaxis::rotary_pick`). The radial relink links the kept pieces.\nThe axis fit, the gouge laws and the verify still read every facet.\n\nA selection that Rotary Parallel cannot use is refused by name: a\npick that is not a face, picks on two models, a face that does not\nlook away from the axis, picks in separate groups, picks no pass\nlies over. Rotary Contour and Rotary Offset refuse a face selection\nby name (#2851, #2852 hold their containment).\n\nThe generation stamp of a rotary operation with a selection gets a\nversion mark, so a path cached under the old reading is stale.\n\nFixes #2848\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
